    <!-- The Gridlink 2x2 mark, light mode. drawable-night/ic_launcher_foreground.xml is the
         canonical variant, ported from the vector master on Talos; this one is derived from
         it and the geometry is identical (cells 19.25, gap 5.5, radius 4.8125, origins 32 and
         56.75). If the geometry moves, move all three: this, the night twin, and the
         monochrome layer.

         🔴 NOT the dark mark on a pale tile. That was the first attempt and it inverts the
         mark: #21405d was chosen to be the quietest thing on near-black, and on near-white it
         becomes the loudest, so the two cells that are supposed to recede end up carrying the
         icon. Every colour here is re-derived by the same rule against the new background
         instead of being reused.

         The rule, from the master: the two diagonal cells are lit and the other two are the
         brand blue at 40% over the tile. "Lit" on black means brighter than the tile, so on
         white it has to mean darker, and the pair inverts:
           dark  top-left #4a90d9 -> bottom-right #7cb2e6  (steps away from black, lighter)
           light top-left #4a90d9 -> bottom-right #35689c  (steps away from white, darker)
         Top-left stays the brand blue exactly in both, so the two variants are recognisably
         the same mark rather than two colourways.

         🔴 Pre-blended, never alpha, same trap as the master. Dim cells are
         rgba(74,144,217,0.4) over the tile resolved by hand: over #06070a that is #21405d,
         over this tile's #f2f6fa midpoint it is #afcdec.

         No bloom layers. The dark variant approximates the master's two feGaussianBlur glows
         with radial gradients; a glow on near-white is invisible at best and grey haze at
         worst, so light simply does without. -->

    <!-- dim cell, top-right -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFAFCDEC"
        android:pathData="M61.5625,32
            h9.625
            a4.8125,4.8125 0 0 1 4.8125,4.8125
            v9.625
            a4.8125,4.8125 0 0 1 -4.8125,4.8125
